Updated ``cryptography`` from 38.0.4 to 50.0.2 (minimum 48.0.1) to fix `GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf <https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf>`__, and updated ``paramiko`` from 2.12.0 to 3.5.1 so it no longer prints ``TripleDES`` deprecation warnings with newer versions of ``cryptography`` (`#68 <https://github.com/sandialabs/PEAT/issues/68>`__). ``paramiko`` stays below 4.0 to keep support for older SSH algorithms that some devices still require. ``cryptography`` no longer publishes wheels for x86_64 macOS or 32-bit Windows, so installing PEAT on those platforms builds ``cryptography`` from source, which requires a Rust toolchain and OpenSSL.
